{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_delivery_overview_reliable_delivery", "label": "Reliable delivery", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/delivery/overview.mdx", "rationale": "tell ist per Default fire-and-forget und kann verloren gehen (gestoppter Empfaenger, Mailbox-Overflow, Netzwerkverlust im Cluster). Die Controller ergaenzen den tell-Vertrag um Sequenznummern und Acks \u2014 fuer Zahlungsanweisungen, Audit-Records, Billing-Events.", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_delivery_overview_producercontroller", "label": "ProducerController (Senderseite)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/delivery/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_delivery_overview_consumercontroller", "label": "ConsumerController (Empfaengerseite)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/delivery/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_delivery_overview_sequence_numbers", "label": "Sequence-number semantics", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/delivery/overview.mdx", "rationale": "Jeder Producer vergibt streng steigende seqs ab 1; Duplikate durch Retransmit tragen dieselbe seq, und die seq ist per-Producer \u2014 mehrere Producer haben unabhaengige seq-Raeume.", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_delivery_overview_at_least_once", "label": "At-least-once", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/delivery/overview.mdx", "rationale": "Der Default: eine Nachricht kann erneut zugestellt werden, wenn der Producer zwischen Senden und Ack-Empfang crasht.", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_delivery_overview_effectively_once", "label": "Effectively-once", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/delivery/overview.mdx", "rationale": "Die In-Memory-Dedup des Controllers deckt den haeufigen Retransmit-vor-Ack-Fall ab; die persistierte Dedup des Handlers deckt Consumer-Crashes mitten in der Verarbeitung ab. Zusammen ergeben sie effectively-once im dauerhaften Sinn. Persistenz auf BEIDEN Seiten gibt Ende-zu-Ende-Garantie; ohne sie faellt die Recovery beidseitig auf null zurueck.", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_delivery_overview_broker_comparison", "label": "In-Cluster-Controller vs externer Broker", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/delivery/overview.mdx", "rationale": "Beide erreichen at-least-once plus Dedup-per-seq. Die Controller haben niedrige Betriebskomplexitaet und sub-Millisekunden-Latenz, sind aber durch die Verarbeitung eines einzelnen Actors durchsatzbegrenzt und cluster-intern; ein Broker skaliert unabhaengig und bedient externe Consumer.", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_delivery_overview_reliable_delivery", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_delivery_overview_producercontroller", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/delivery/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_delivery_overview_reliable_delivery", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_delivery_overview_consumercontroller", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/delivery/overview.mdx", "source_locatio